{
  "total": 145,
  "totalPage": 3,
  "page": 3,
  "pageSize": 50,
  "items": [
    {
      "id": "69b6c859dd1a4c9c86f0c8b2",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 7,
      "hadithIndex": 1738,
      "bookHadithIndex": 101,
      "text": "It was narrated from Abu Qatadah that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“Fasting the day of ‘Ashura’, I hope, will expiate for the sins of the previous year.”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1738-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1738-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1738-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c859dd1a4c9c86f0c8b3",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 7,
      "hadithIndex": 1739,
      "bookHadithIndex": 102,
      "text": "It was narrated from Rabi’ah bin Ghaz that he asked ‘Aishah about the fasting of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). She said:“He used to make sure he fasted on Mondays and Thursdays.”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1739-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1739-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1739-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c859dd1a4c9c86f0c8b4",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 7,
      "hadithIndex": 1740,
      "bookHadithIndex": 103,
      "text": "It was narrated from Abu Hurairah that the Prophet (ﷺ) used to fast on Mondays and Thursdays. It was said:“O Messenger of Allah, why do you fast on Mondays and Thursdays?” He said: “On Mondays and Thursdays Allah forgives every Muslim except two who have forsaken one another. He says: ‘Leave these two until they reconcile.’”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1740-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1740-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1740-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c859dd1a4c9c86f0c8b5",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 7,
      "hadithIndex": 1741,
      "bookHadithIndex": 104,
      "text": "It was narrated from Abu Mujibah Al-Bahili that his father or, his paternal uncle, said:“I came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said: ‘O Prophet of Allah, I am the man who came to you last year.’ He said: ‘Why do I see your body so thin (and weak)?’ He said: ‘O Messenger of Allah! I do not eat during the day; I only eat at night.’ He said: ‘Who commanded you to punish yourself?’ I said: ‘O Messenger of Allah! I am strong enough.’ He said: ‘Fast the month of patience* and one day after it.’ I said: ‘I am strong enough (to do more).’ He said: ‘Fast the month of patience and two days after it.’ I said: ‘I am strong enough (to do more).’ He said: ‘Fast the month of patience and three days after it, and fast the sacred months.’”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1741-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1741-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1741-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1741-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c859dd1a4c9c86f0c8b6",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 7,
      "hadithIndex": 1742,
      "bookHadithIndex": 105,
      "text": "It was narrated that Abu Hurairah said:“A man came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said: ‘Which fasting is better after the month of Ramadan?’ He said: ‘The month of Allah which is called Muharram.’”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1742-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1742-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1742-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Muslim"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c859dd1a4c9c86f0c8b7",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 7,
      "hadithIndex": 1743,
      "bookHadithIndex": 106,
      "text": "It was narrated from Ibn ‘Abbas that:The Prophet (ﷺ) forbade fasting Rajab",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1743-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Very Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1743-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Very Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1743-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1743-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c859dd1a4c9c86f0c8b8",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 7,
      "hadithIndex": 1744,
      "bookHadithIndex": 107,
      "text": "It was narrated from Muhammad bin Ibrahim that Usamah bin Zaid used to fast the sacred months. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to him:“Fast Shawwal.” So he forsook the sacred months and he continued to fast Shawwal until he died",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1744-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1744-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1744-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1744-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c859dd1a4c9c86f0c8b9",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 7,
      "hadithIndex": 1745,
      "bookHadithIndex": 108,
      "text": "It was narrated from Abu Hurairah that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“For everything there is Zakat and the Zakat of the body is fasting.” (A narrator in one of the chains) Muhriz added in his narration: \"And the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Fasting is half of patience",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1745-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1745-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1745-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1745-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c859dd1a4c9c86f0c8ba",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 7,
      "hadithIndex": 1746,
      "bookHadithIndex": 109,
      "text": "It was narrated from Zaid bin Khalid Al-Juhani that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“Whoever gives food for a fasting person to break his fast, he will have a reward like theirs, without that detracting from their reward in the slightest.”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1746-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1746-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1746-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1746-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c859dd1a4c9c86f0c8bb",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 7,
      "hadithIndex": 1747,
      "bookHadithIndex": 110,
      "text": "It was narrated that ‘Abdullah bin Zubair said:“The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) broke his fast with Sa’d bin Mu’adh and said: ‘Aftara ‘indakumus-saimun, wa akala ta’amakumul-abrar, wa sallat ‘alaikumul- mala’ikah (May fasting people break their fast with you, may the righteous eat your food, and may the angels send blessing upon you).”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1747-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1747-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1747-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih Lighairihi"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1747-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c859dd1a4c9c86f0c8bc",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 7,
      "hadithIndex": 1748,
      "bookHadithIndex": 111,
      "text": "It was narrated that Umm ‘Umarah said:“The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came to us and we brought food for him. Some of those who were with him were fasting, and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ‘If food is eaten in the presence of one who is fasting, the angels send blessing upon him.’”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1748-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1748-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1748-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1748-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c859dd1a4c9c86f0c8bd",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 7,
      "hadithIndex": 1749,
      "bookHadithIndex": 112,
      "text": "It was narrated from Sulaiman bin Buraidah that his father said:“The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to Bilal: ‘Come and eat, O Bilal.’ He said: ‘I am fasting.’ The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ‘We are eating our provision, but most of Bilal’s provision is in Paradise. Do you realise, O Bilal, that the bones of the fasting person glorify Allah and the angels pray for forgiveness for him so long as food is eaten in front of him?’”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1749-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Mawdu"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1749-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Mawdu"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1749-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Mawdu"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1749-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c859dd1a4c9c86f0c8be",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 7,
      "hadithIndex": 1750,
      "bookHadithIndex": 113,
      "text": "It was narrated from Abu Hurairah that the Prophet (ﷺ) said:“If anyone of you is invited to eat when he is fasting, let him say: ‘I am fasting.’”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1750-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1750-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1750-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1750-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Muslim"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c859dd1a4c9c86f0c8bf",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 7,
      "hadithIndex": 1751,
      "bookHadithIndex": 114,
      "text": "It was narrated from Jabir that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“Whoever is invited to eat when he is fasting, let him accept the invitation; and if he wants to let him eat, and if he wants let him not eat.”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1751-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1751-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1751-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1751-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c859dd1a4c9c86f0c8c0",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 7,
      "hadithIndex": 1752,
      "bookHadithIndex": 115,
      "text": "It was narrated from Abu Hurairah that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:There are three whose supplications are not turned back: A just ruler, and a fasting person until he breaks his fast. And, the supplication of one who has been wronged is raised by Allah up to the clouds on the Day of Resurrection, and the gates of heaven are opened for it, and Allah says, ‘By My Might I will help you (against the wrongdoer) even if it is after a while.’”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1752-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1752-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1752-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1752-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c859dd1a4c9c86f0c8c1",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 7,
      "hadithIndex": 1753,
      "bookHadithIndex": 116,
      "text": "It was narrated from ‘Abdullah bin ‘Amr bin ‘As that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“When the fasting person breaks his fast, his supplication is not turned back.” (One of the narrators) Ibn Abi Mulaikah said: \"When he broke his fast, I heard 'Abdullah bin 'Amr say: 'O Allah! I ask You by Your mercy, which encompasses all things, to forgive me",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1753-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1753-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1753-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1753-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c859dd1a4c9c86f0c8c2",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 7,
      "hadithIndex": 1754,
      "bookHadithIndex": 117,
      "text": "It was narrated that Anas bin Malik said:“The Prophet (ﷺ) would not go out on the Day of Fitr until he had eaten some dates.”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1754-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1754-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1754-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1754-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Bukhari"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c859dd1a4c9c86f0c8c3",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 7,
      "hadithIndex": 1755,
      "bookHadithIndex": 118,
      "text": "It was narrated that Ibn ‘Umar said:“The Prophet (ﷺ) would not go out on the Day of Fitr until he had had given his Companions some of the charity of Fitr to eat.”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1755-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1755-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1755-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1755-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c859dd1a4c9c86f0c8c4",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 7,
      "hadithIndex": 1756,
      "bookHadithIndex": 119,
      "text": "It was narrated from Ibn Buraidah from his father, that:The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) would not go out on the Day of Fitr until he had eaten, and he would not eat on the Day of Nahr (the day of sacrifice) until he came back",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1756-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1756-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1756-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih Lighairihi"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1756-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c859dd1a4c9c86f0c8c5",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 7,
      "hadithIndex": 1757,
      "bookHadithIndex": 120,
      "text": "It was narrated from Ibn ‘Umar that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:‘Whoever dies owing the fasts of a month, one poor person should be fed on his behalf for each day.”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1757-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1757-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1757-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c859dd1a4c9c86f0c8c6",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 7,
      "hadithIndex": 1758,
      "bookHadithIndex": 121,
      "text": "It was narrated that Ibn ‘Abbas said:“A woman came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said: ‘O Messenger of Allah, my sister has died and she owed a fast of two consecutive months.’ He said: ‘Do you not think that if your sister owed a debt, you would pay it off for her?’ She said: ‘Of course.’ He said: ‘The right of Allah is greater.’”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1758-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1758-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1758-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Bukhari And Muslim"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c859dd1a4c9c86f0c8c7",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 7,
      "hadithIndex": 1759,
      "bookHadithIndex": 122,
      "text": "It was narrated from Ibn Buraidah that his father said:“A woman came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said: ‘O Messenger of Allah, my mother has died and she owed a fast. Should I fast on her behalf?’ He said: ‘Yes.’”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1759-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1759-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1759-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1759-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Muslim"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c859dd1a4c9c86f0c8c8",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 7,
      "hadithIndex": 1760,
      "bookHadithIndex": 123,
      "text": "It was narrated that ‘Atiyyah bin Sufyan bin ‘Abdullah bin Rabi’ah said:“Our delegation who went to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) to announce the Islam of Thaqif told us that they came to him in Ramadan. He set up a tent for them in the mosque, and when they became Muslim, they fasted what was left of the month.”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1760-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1760-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1760-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1760-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c859dd1a4c9c86f0c8c9",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 7,
      "hadithIndex": 1761,
      "bookHadithIndex": 124,
      "text": "It was narrated from Abu Hurairah that the Prophet (ﷺ) said:“When her husband is present, no woman should fast any day apart from the month of Ramadan without his permission.”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1761-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1761-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1761-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1761-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c859dd1a4c9c86f0c8ca",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 7,
      "hadithIndex": 1762,
      "bookHadithIndex": 125,
      "text": "It was narrated that Abu Sa’eed said:“The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade women from fasting without the permission of their husbands.”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1762-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1762-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1762-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1762-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c859dd1a4c9c86f0c8cb",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 7,
      "hadithIndex": 1763,
      "bookHadithIndex": 126,
      "text": "It was narrated from ‘Aishah that the Prophet (ﷺ) said:“If a man stays among a people, he should not fast without their permission.”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1763-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Very Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1763-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Very Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1763-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1763-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c859dd1a4c9c86f0c8cc",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 7,
      "hadithIndex": 1764,
      "bookHadithIndex": 127,
      "text": "It was narrated from Abu Hurairah that the Prophet (ﷺ) said:“A grateful eater is equal to a patient fasting person.”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1764-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1764-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1764-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c859dd1a4c9c86f0c8cd",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 7,
      "hadithIndex": 1765,
      "bookHadithIndex": 128,
      "text": "It was narrated from Sinan bin Sannah Al-Aslami, the Companion of the Prophet (ﷺ), that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“A grateful eater will have a reward like that of a patient fasting person.”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1765-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1765-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1765-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c859dd1a4c9c86f0c8ce",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 7,
      "hadithIndex": 1766,
      "bookHadithIndex": 129,
      "text": "It was narrated that Abu Sa’eed Al-Khudri said:“We observed I’tikaf with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) during the middle ten days of Ramadan. He said: ‘I have been shown Lailatul-Qadr, then I was caused to forget it, so seek it in the last ten night, on the odd-numbered nights.’”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1766-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1766-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1766-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1766-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Bukhari And Muslim"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c859dd1a4c9c86f0c8cf",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 7,
      "hadithIndex": 1767,
      "bookHadithIndex": 130,
      "text": "It was narrated that ‘Aishah said:“The Prophet (ﷺ) used to strive hard (in worship) in the last ten nights of Ramadan as he never did at any other time.”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1767-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1767-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1767-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1767-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Muslim"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c859dd1a4c9c86f0c8d0",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 7,
      "hadithIndex": 1768,
      "bookHadithIndex": 131,
      "text": "It was narrated that ‘Aishah said:“When the last ten days of Ramadan began, the Prophet (ﷺ) used to stay up at night, tighten his waist- wrap, and wake up his family (to pray).”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1768-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1768-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1768-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1768-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Bukhari And Muslim"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c859dd1a4c9c86f0c8d1",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 7,
      "hadithIndex": 1769,
      "bookHadithIndex": 132,
      "text": "It was narrated that Abu Hurairah said:“The Prophet (ﷺ) used to observe I’tikaf for ten days every year. In the year in which he passed away, he observed I’tikaf for twenty days. And the Qur’an would be reviewed with him once every year, but in the year in which he passed away, it was reviewed with him twice.”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1769-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1769-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1769-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1769-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Bukhari"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c859dd1a4c9c86f0c8d2",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 7,
      "hadithIndex": 1770,
      "bookHadithIndex": 133,
      "text": "It was narrated from Ubayy bin Ka’b that:The Prophet (ﷺ) used to spend the last ten days of Ramadan in I’tikaf. One year he was traveling, so the following year he spent twenty days in I’tikaf",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1770-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1770-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1770-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1770-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c859dd1a4c9c86f0c8d3",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 7,
      "hadithIndex": 1771,
      "bookHadithIndex": 134,
      "text": "It was narrated that ‘Aishah said:“When the Prophet (ﷺ) wanted to start I’tikaf, he would pray the Subh, then he would enter the place where he wanted to observe I’tikaf. He wanted to spend the last ten days of Ramadan in I’tikaf, so he ordered that a tent be set up for him.” Then ‘Aishah ordered that a tent be set up for her, and Hafash ordered that a tent be set up for her. When Zainab saw their two tents, she also ordered that a tent be set up for her. When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saw that, he said: “It is righteousness that you seek?” Then he did not observe I’tikaf during Ramadan, and he observed I’tikaf during ten days of Shawwal",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1771-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1771-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1771-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1771-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Bukhari And Muslim"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c859dd1a4c9c86f0c8d4",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 7,
      "hadithIndex": 1772,
      "bookHadithIndex": 135,
      "text": "It was narrated from ‘Umar that he had vowed during the days of Ignorance to spend one night in I’tikaf. He asked the Prophet (ﷺ) about it, so he commanded him to spend it in I’tikaf",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1772-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1772-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1772-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Bukhari And Muslim"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c859dd1a4c9c86f0c8d5",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 7,
      "hadithIndex": 1773,
      "bookHadithIndex": 136,
      "text": "It was narrated from ‘Abdullah bin ‘Umar that:The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to spend the last ten days of Ramadan in I’tikaf. Nafi' said: \" Abdullah bin 'Umar showed me the place where the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to observe I'tikaf",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1773-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1773-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1773-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Bukhari And Muslim"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c859dd1a4c9c86f0c8d6",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 7,
      "hadithIndex": 1774,
      "bookHadithIndex": 137,
      "text": "It was narrated from Ibn ‘Umar that:When the Prophet (ﷺ) observed I’tikaf, his bedding would be spread for him, or his bed would be placed there for him, behind the Pillar of Repentance",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1774-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1774-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1774-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1774-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c859dd1a4c9c86f0c8d7",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 7,
      "hadithIndex": 1775,
      "bookHadithIndex": 138,
      "text": "It was narrated from Abu Sa’eed Al-Khudri that:The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) observed I’tifak in a Turkish tent, over the door of which was a piece of reed matting. He pushed the mat aside, then he put his head out and spoke to the people",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1775-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1775-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1775-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1775-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Muslim"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c859dd1a4c9c86f0c8d8",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 7,
      "hadithIndex": 1776,
      "bookHadithIndex": 139,
      "text": "It was narrated that ‘Aishah said:“I used to enter the house to relieve myself, and there was a sick person there, and I only inquired after him as I was passing through.” She said: “And the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) would not enter the house except to relieve himself, then they were observing I’tikaf.”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1776-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1776-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1776-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1776-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Bukhari"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c859dd1a4c9c86f0c8d9",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 7,
      "hadithIndex": 1777,
      "bookHadithIndex": 140,
      "text": "It was narrated that Anas bin Malik said:“The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ‘The person observing I’tikaf may attend funerals and visit the sick.’”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1777-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Mawdu"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1777-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Mawdu"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1777-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c859dd1a4c9c86f0c8da",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 7,
      "hadithIndex": 1778,
      "bookHadithIndex": 141,
      "text": "It was narrated that ‘Aishah said:“The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to bring his head towards me when he was next door (observing I’tikaf), and I would wash it and comb his hair, when I was in my apartment and I was menstruating, and he was in the mosque.”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1778-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1778-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1778-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1778-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c859dd1a4c9c86f0c8db",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 7,
      "hadithIndex": 1779,
      "bookHadithIndex": 142,
      "text": "It was narrated from Safiyyah bint Huyai, the wife of the Prophet (ﷺ), that she came to visit the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) when he was in I’tikaf during the last ten days of the month of Ramadan. She spoke with him for a while during the evening, then she stood up to go back. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) got up to take her home. When she reached the door of the mosque that was by the home of Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet (ﷺ), two men from among the Ansar passed by them. They greeted the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) with peace, then went away. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“Take it easy, she is Safiyyah bint Huyai.” They said: “Glorious is Allah, O Messenger of Allah!” And they were very upset by that (i.e., that he thought they may have some doubts). The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “The Satan flows through the son of Adam like blood, and I was afraid that he might cast some doubt into your hearts.”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1779-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1779-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1779-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Bukhari And Muslim"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c859dd1a4c9c86f0c8dc",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 7,
      "hadithIndex": 1780,
      "bookHadithIndex": 143,
      "text": "‘Aishah said:“One of the wives of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) observed I’tikaf with him, and she used to see red and yellow discharge, and sometime she would put a basin beneath her.”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1780-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1780-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1780-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1780-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Bukhari"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c859dd1a4c9c86f0c8dd",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 7,
      "hadithIndex": 1781,
      "bookHadithIndex": 144,
      "text": "It was narrated from Ibn ‘Abbas that:The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said concerning the person observing I’tikaf. “He is refraining from sin and he will be given a reward like that of one who does all kinds of good deeds.”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1781-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1781-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1781-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1781-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c859dd1a4c9c86f0c8de",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 7,
      "hadithIndex": 1782,
      "bookHadithIndex": 145,
      "text": "It was narrated from Abu Umamah that the Prophet (ﷺ) said:“Whoever spends the nights of the two ‘Eid in praying voluntary prayers, seeking reward from Allah, his heart will not die on the Day when hearts will die.”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1782-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Mawdu"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1782-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Mawdu"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-7-1782-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}